------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Presentations of groups
--
-- Proposition B.3: the theory is complete on three wires, and G₃ ≅ S₈
--
-- Our wire 2 is the paper's x₁, wire 1 its x₂ and wire 0 its x₃.  The
-- states, in the Gray order 000, 001, 011, 010, 110, 111, 101, 100
-- (x₁x₂x₃), are numbered by enc, and T d, the edge Toffoli of the states
-- d and d + 1, realises their transposition.  An edge Toffoli is spelled
-- by its direction (target wire) and the values of its two controls,
-- with X around a control whose value is 0:
--
--   direction 0:  CCX                     (controls on wires 2, 1)
--   direction 1:  σ CCX σ                 (controls on wires 2, 0)
--   direction 2:  σ ↑ σ CCX σ σ ↑         (controls on wires 1, 0)
--
-- The Coxeter relations follow Appendix B.  Lemma B.4 in direction 0:
-- T4 T2 and T4 T6 are the CNOTs into wire 0 (rule (4), with (5)), the two
-- ways of writing X on wire 0 as a product of the four edge Toffolis of
-- direction 0 (rule (2) on the wires 1, 0 and 2, 0) show that they
-- commute, and X on wire 0 commutes with each (X0T4⁼).  The same for the
-- other directions by swaps (X1T5⁼, X2B⁼).  Conjugating an edge Toffoli
-- by X on a wire or by an adjacent swap gives another edge Toffoli
-- (cj…⁼, sixty lemmas).  Lemma B.5's two base relations are far14⁼
-- (from (6): T1 commutes with T4) and braid4⁼ (from (6) and (3)), and
-- every other Coxeter relation is one of them carried by a symmetry of
-- the cube (a word in X's and swaps), through those conjugations.  The
-- gates are words in the T d (Prop. B.3's proof: X on wire 0 is
-- T4 T2 T6 T0, CX is T2 T4, the swap of wires 0, 1 is CX (T1 T5) CX,
-- and the rest by swaps), and ByCoxeter concludes.
--
-- The lemmas are generated by gen/width3.py (the derivations) and
-- gen/mk_width3.py (this module); every step is a rule of the theory, a
-- swap rule, a two-wire step justified by completeness on two wires
-- (Narrow2.by2), or the commutation of letters on disjoint wires.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

